 "summary": "All three prior public-API findings are met at the current head: the unconditional `cosAngle_eq_energy_mul_sub_div` covers the massive pseudojets Layer 2 consumes, the `Bilin` API is single-homed in `Kinematics.Bilin` with no forwarding surface, and the frame-rescaling invariance lemmas remove the practical cost of `0 < g n n` (which the roadmap specifies verbatim). Bodies are unexposed with `(rfl)` def-lemmas and pointwise `_apply` characterisations, nothing is `private`, and the simp annotations are correct.",
